---
import PageLayout from '../../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Section from '../../../components/Section.astro';
import Card from '../../../components/Card.astro';
---
<PageLayout
  title="Join Our Troop"
  description="How to join Trail Life Troop TX-0521: registration, dues, medical forms, and uniform."
  eyebrow="Trail Life Troop TX-0521"
  heading="Join Our Troop"
  heroImage="/images/join-hero.jpg"
  heroAlt="Mountain sunset scenery"
>
  <Section tone="cream" class="narrow-content">
    <p>We're so glad you're considering joining our troop! Here, we desire to point everything to Christ, and we are committed to growing together in faith, leadership, character, and a heart for service. Together, we'll focus on developing young men who honor God in all they do, while building lifelong friendships and memorable experiences. Ready to embark on this journey with us? Let's get started!</p>
    <p>To join our troop and begin this exciting journey, we've outlined a few simple steps. From registration to purchasing uniforms, we'll guide you through everything you need to know to get started with confidence and ease.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="light" class="centered-heading">
    <h2>Step 1: Register on TrailLifeConnect.com</h2>
    <p>Start by visiting <a href="https://www.traillifeconnect.com/register/tkbapf3m5536" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">TrailLifeConnect.com</a> to create an account for the parent. Once your account is set up, click the Add Son button to create a profile for your son. After the profile is complete, you'll be prompted to pay the national fee for that child. If you have multiple sons, simply repeat the process for each one.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="cream" class="centered-heading">
    <h2>Step 2: Pay Troop Dues</h2>
    <p>After you've created the accounts, <a href="/about#dues">meet with our troop treasurer to pay your dues</a>. You can pay by cash, check (made payable to Trail Life TX-0521), or <a href="https://www.zeffy.com/en-US/ticketing/trail-life-tx--0521" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Zeffy</a>. The treasurer will assist you in completing the payment and answer any questions right there.</p>
    <p>Please note, if using Zeffy, in order to keep their platform free for nonprofits, they default to a 17% contribution. You do have the option to change this to any value you consider appropriate. Be sure to select <strong>Other</strong> instead of 17% and enter a dollar amount in the Contribution field.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="light" class="centered-heading">
    <h2>Step 3: Complete Medical Forms</h2>
    <p>Each adult and trailman will need to fill out a medical form. You can download the forms using the links below, print them, and bring them to the next meeting. If you're attending our open house event, we'll have forms available to fill out in person.</p>
    <p><a href="https://www.traillifeconnect.com/getdoc/dockwq07qk4a" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Download Youth Medical Form</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp; <a href="https://www.traillifeconnect.com/getdoc/docgs3xlkcv8" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Download Adult Medical Form</a></p>
    <p>If you have medical insurance, please provide a copy of both the front and back of your insurance card with each form.</p>
    <p>Trail Life USA no longer requires immunizations, though they are still recommended. Exemption requests are no longer necessary.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="cream" class="centered-heading">
    <h2>Step 4: Purchase Your Uniform</h2>
    <p>Each trailman needs to have the official troop uniform, which includes a troop shirt, lanyard, and shoulder loops. They'll also need a tri-color hat.</p>
    <p><a href="https://shop.traillifeusa.com/product/troop-uniform-build-your-own-bundle" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Troop Uniform Bundle</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp; <a href="https://shop.traillifeusa.com/product/tri-color-hat" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Tri-Color Hat</a></p>
    <p>For more details on the uniform and our troop's requirements, visit our <a href="/about/uniforms">uniform page</a>.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="light" class="centered-heading">
    <h2>Further Steps</h2>
    <p>Once you've completed the initial steps, there are a few more ways you can get involved and learn more about the Trail Life experience.</p>
    <div class="card-grid card-grid-2">
      <Card variant="surface">
        <h3>Learn More About Trail Life</h3>
        <p>Log into <a href="https://traillifeconnect.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">TrailLifeConnect.com</a> and click the Welcome to Trail Life and Basecamp buttons for additional reading on the program and its values.</p>
      </Card>
      <Card variant="surface">
        <h3>Get Involved with the Troop</h3>
        <p>Become a Registered Adult! This process includes a criminal background check and youth protection training, ensuring a safe and supportive environment for all our Trailmen. We encourage all our parents to become Registered Adults. If you're interested, reach out to leadership to start the process.</p>
      </Card>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <section class="join">
    <div>
      <h2>We're Excited to Have You!</h2>
      <p>Keep an eye on upcoming events, and don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions. We look forward to growing together in faith, fellowship, and adventure.</p>
      <a class="button button-light" href="/contact">Contact</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
